From 866539dfd873115d452e6166bfc81bd70b4f8f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anonymous <anonymous@invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Speed hint: let the running program know it is being
 fast-forwarded

While the sound clock is scaled (fast-forward or slow motion with "Keep
music at normal speed" on), a 32-bit read of 0x04FFFA40 returns 0x5350
("SP") in the upper half and the current speed in 8.8 fixed point in the
lower half (0x0100 = normal speed). The address is unused on hardware;
there and in other emulators it reads 0.

Sounds now keep real time during fast-forward, so a game that waits for
a fanfare or a cry to end holds the sped-up game for the sound's full
length. With this hint a game (for example a ROM hack) can skip such
waits while fast-forwarding and behave as before everywhere else.
---
 src/NDS.cpp                              | 8 ++++++++
 src/NDS.h                                | 9 +++++++++
 src/frontend/qt_sdl/EmuInstanceAudio.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

